WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.980
A shrew is among the smallest mammals.

2
00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:06.280
A deer has thousands of times more mass.

3
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:12.070
Yet look inside both, and their cells of
a given type are of broadly similar size.

4
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.120
A large animal is not made of giant cells.

5
00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:17.790
It is made of many more small ones.

6
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:21.030
So why are almost all
cells too small to see,

7
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.700
even inside the largest animals?

8
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.210
In this mission, you'll model cells as
cubes and compare their surface with their

9
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:29.250
volume.

10
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:34.610
Then you'll work out exactly what happens
to both as a cube doubles in size.

11
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.250
Your mission: explain why almost
all cells are too small to see,

12
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.400
even inside the largest animals.
